SUMMARY:[Machine Learning][Deep Representation Learning] LoG 2026 - Confere
 nce
DESCRIPTION:Conference title: Learning on Graphs Conference\nWebsite: https
 ://logconference.org/\nSource URL: https://logconference.org/\nLocation: 
 Boston\, Massachusetts\, USA\nTopics: Machine Learning\, Deep Representat
 ion Learning\, Complex Systems & Network Science\, Learning Theory & Stat
 istical Foundations\nSize: M\nSubmission type: Paper-based / non-archival
  extended abstracts\nConfidence: confirmed\nLast checked date: 2026-10-07
 \nNotes: Fifth annual edition\, in person at Northeastern University. Ext
 ended Aug 5/7 deadlines replace the struck-through July 29/Aug 1 dates. P
 roceedings papers and non-archival extended abstracts share the registrat
 ion and final submission cutoffs\, represented as one route. The TMLR pre
 sentation track requires an already published paper\, so it is not a new-
 paper opportunity. LoG is distinct from LOD/AIS. Size M is an editorial e
 stimate.\nScope: Learning on graphs and geometry: graph neural networks\,
  equivariant models\, graph kernels\, geometric and graph generative mode
 ls\, and statistical theory for structured data. Graph signal processing\
 , causal graph models\, robustness\, and scalable graph-learning infrastr
 ucture are meaningful extensions. A graph or geometric contribution shoul
 d remain central\, even in an application such as language or molecular m
 odeling.\nAdditional topics: Probabilistic\, Causal & Uncertainty ML\, Si
 gnal Processing\, Robustness & Safety\, ML Systems & Infrastructure\nScop
 e sources (2026): https://logconference.org/cfp/\nScope last checked: 202
 6-10-07
URL:https://logconference.org/
LOCATION:Boston\, Massachusetts\, USA
END:VEVENT
